From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:49:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(notices): pin lane-through-generation order; drop unused
 _decoded fallback [daveey]

Follow-up to #1768 review nits.

- New deterministic interleaving test: an older snapshot's poller is gated at
  each post-read publication-lock entry until it owns the replica lane with the
  newer poller blocked on it (or the newer poller finished). Generations must
  follow snapshot order and the newer snapshot's memo must be the one published.
- `_snapshot`/`_changed_rows_cards` now require the caller's decode map:
  observe always passes the per-lane `_ReplicaFlight.decoded`, so the
  module-level `_decoded` fallback had no production caller. The direct-helper
  bounded-read test passes its own map; `_reset_for_tests` stops clearing it.
- Stray blank lines removed.

Proof: mutants (each x4 runs, no flaky retry pass) all fail the new test:
  block_out (signature check + generation moved after the lane),
  gen_out (only generation moved after the lane),
  no_gen_check (publish regardless of generation).
32 test files importing kanban_remote_{observations,notices}: 462 passed.
